  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Astable and monostable modes"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "*Astable*: $R_A$, $R_B$ and C are connected so that C charges through $R_A + R_B$ from $\\tfrac13V_{CC}$ to $\\tfrac23V_{CC}$ (output high, $t_H = 0.693(R_A + R_B)C$) and discharges through $R_B$ into pin 7 (output low, $t_L = 0.693R_BC$). So $f = 1.44/[(R_A + 2R_B)C]$ and the duty cycle $D = (R_A + R_B)/(R_A + 2R_B)$, always above 50%. Monostable: a trigger pulse at pin 2 below $\\tfrac13V_{CC}$ sets the output high; C charges through R until $\\tfrac23V_{CC}$, giving a pulse of width $T = 1.1RC$."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "tH = 0.693(RA + RB)C; tL = 0.693RB·C"
    },
    {
     "en": "f = 1.44/((RA + 2RB)C)"
    },
    {
     "en": "Duty cycle (RA + RB)/(RA + 2RB) > 50%"
    },
    {
     "en": "*Monostable* pulse T = 1.1RC"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "In astable mode the frequency is 1.44 over RA plus twice RB, times C. In monostable mode one trigger gives a pulse of 1.1 R C.",
    "kn": "ಅಸ್ಥಿರ ವಿಧಾನದಲ್ಲಿ f = 1.44/((RA + 2RB)C). ಏಕಸ್ಥಿರ ವಿಧಾನದಲ್ಲಿ ಒಂದು ಟ್ರಿಗರ್ T = 1.1RC ಅಗಲದ ಪಲ್ಸ್ ನೀಡುತ್ತದೆ."
   },
